# Shell scripts must be LF, always.
#
# The container entrypoint is authored on Windows and read by /bin/sh inside a
# Linux image. A CRLF shebang fails as `/bin/sh\r: not found`, an error that
# names neither the file nor the cause. The Dockerfile strips carriage returns
# as a second line of defence; this is the first.
*.sh text eol=lf
